## [ENT-109] | 2026-11-18 00:36 UTC | Apollo | error | ref: game/routes/guidebook/logistics.md | see: orders.log ENT-052
Class: an engine call written from the game's help text instead of copied from a script that flies it (the class of ENT-098, repeated: that fix was a pitfall in my skill, a rule to remember, not a check).
Case: on 2026-11-18 my office probe (orders ENT-052, block APOLLO (4): does an outpost take a faction office) was to read `facility types` category faction with a member hauler docked at our outpost, caught at the end of the bunker supply run. I wrote the call from the help of `spacemolt_facility`, whose heading reads "## facility" with a parameter `action` (types, faction_list ...), as toolGroup spacemolt_facility, action `facility`, params {"action": "types"}. The gate answered 500 "unknown action facility" at 00:32 UTC for both reads. build.py of my own skill, which flew faction_build three times on 2026-11-17, calls the sub-action itself as the action (`faction_build`, `faction_list`).
Effect: the probe missed its first chance; the hauler left the outpost on its next route at 00:33 UTC. No credit lost, no ship harmed. The read waits for the next bunker run (two runs left in its budget); the driver is started again with the corrected call.
Cause: a call nobody of mine had flown in that form went into a catch row without its first flight by hand (rule F29: the first flight of a call is one ship by hand), and the help's heading was read as the action name.
Fix, done: the probe calls `types` and `faction_list` as actions, the form flown at 00:36 UTC on a free docked hauler (http 200, 56 faction facility types, page 1 of 3); the skill logistics-stock's pitfall now says that the gate's `action` is the sub-action the help lists under Actions, and that a call a driver makes is flown once with the tool command on a free docked pilot before the driver starts.
Would it have prevented this one: yes, the first flight by hand would have shown the 500 before the catch row ran.

