## [ENT-111] | 2026-11-21 20:05 UTC | Zero | error | ref: game/routes/mine-achernar-frost-ring-nexus.json | see: orders.log ENT-056
Class: a rule kept only where a turn reads it, while a gate fires between turns (the family of ENT-106 and ENT-108).
Case: at the resume of 2026-11-21 the Central Nexus book bid water ice 28 cr for 371 units (data/market/central_nexus.json, 19:48 UTC), above the 300-unit gate (requires.bid) of five Central Nexus ice mine routes of the template ice-sell. Six miners took those mine routes (fleet file, 19:56 UTC), while Mining stored 18,541 water ice (table stock_hour, 18:00 UTC) and two drain-ice-nexus runs had already sold stored ice into the same bid (+2,156 cr).
Effect: about six ship-runs of fuel for ice the stores could have sold; what the bid does not take is stored again. No ship harmed.
Cause: "stored ice is sold before new ice is mined" stands in my turn skill (divide the stored ice by what the bids regain) and in my knowledge file; the route's own gate counts only the bid's depth, so between turns nothing applies the rule.
Fix, done: requires.bid min_qty 300 -> 3,000 on the five routes (a deep order the stored ice cannot fill within a turn), the template note says so. Proposed in my report: a route field that opens a mine route only while the division's stored units of its good stand under a number, so the rule fires by itself.
Would it have prevented this one: the raised gate, yes for a bid of 371 units; the proposed field, yes for any bid.

